# {{.AppName}} Deployment Guide

This project uses Pay Theory-style deployment (CodeBuild + shell scripts).

## Prerequisites

- AWS CLI configured with appropriate credentials
- AWS CDK CLI installed (`npm install -g aws-cdk`)
- Go 1.25 or later
- Node.js 20 or later

## Environment Variables

The deployment system uses these environment variables:

| Variable | Required | Description |
|----------|----------|-------------|
| `PARTNER` | Yes | Partner identifier for multi-tenant isolation |
| `STAGE` | Yes | Deployment stage: `dev`, `staging`, or `live` |
| `TARGET_MODE` | No | Deployment mode (default: `standard`) |
| `AWS_REGION` | No | AWS region (auto-detected if not set) |

## Local Development

### Initialize Environment

```bash
source ./shell/init_env_vars.sh
```

Edit the file to set your `PARTNER` value before sourcing.

### Build Lambda Functions

```bash
./shell/build.sh
```

### Deploy

```bash
# Deploy to dev
./shell/deploy.sh --partner mypartner --stage dev

# Deploy to staging
./shell/deploy.sh --partner mypartner --stage staging

# Deploy to production
./shell/deploy.sh --partner mypartner --stage live
```

### Other Commands

```bash
# Show what would change
./shell/deploy.sh --partner mypartner --stage dev --command diff

# Synthesize CloudFormation templates
./shell/deploy.sh --partner mypartner --stage dev --command synth

# Destroy deployment
./shell/deploy.sh --partner mypartner --stage dev --command destroy

# Bootstrap CDK (first-time setup)
./shell/deploy.sh --partner mypartner --stage dev --command bootstrap
```

### Using `lift` CLI

You can also use the `lift` CLI with partner context:

```bash
# Build all functions
lift build

# Deploy to dev with partner
lift up --stage dev --partner mypartner

# Destroy
lift down --stage dev --partner mypartner
```

## CodeBuild Integration

This project includes a `buildspec.yml` for AWS CodeBuild. It expects:

1. CodeBuild environment variables set:
   - `PARTNER`
   - `STAGE`
   - `TARGET_MODE` (optional, defaults to `standard`)
   - `AWS_REGION`

2. IAM permissions for:
   - CDK bootstrap resources
   - CloudFormation stack management
   - Lambda deployment
   - API Gateway management
   - DynamoDB (if used)
   - Other resources as defined in CDK

## Stack Naming

Stacks are named with the pattern: `{{.AppName}}-service-<partner>-<stage>`

Example: `{{.AppName}}-service-mypartner-dev`

## Stages

| Stage | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| `dev` | Development environment |
| `staging` | Staging/QA environment |
| `live` | Production environment |

## Troubleshooting

### CDK Bootstrap Required

If you see "CDK bootstrap required" error:

```bash
./shell/deploy.sh --partner mypartner --stage dev --command bootstrap
```

### Missing Permissions

Ensure your AWS credentials have permissions to:
- Create/update CloudFormation stacks
- Deploy Lambda functions
- Create API Gateway resources
- Access other AWS services used by your stack

### Build Failures

Check Go module dependencies:

```bash
go mod tidy
go mod verify
```
